   <div class="col-lg-8">
         <div class="blog-content">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="TNPSC Combined Technical Services (CTC) Exam Dates 2026 – Complete Schedule">
             <div class="blog-body">
                 <h1 class="blog-title">TNPSC Combined Technical Services (CTC) Exam Dates 2026 – Your Complete Schedule Guide!</h1>

                 <p>Aspiring candidates for government jobs in Tamil Nadu, gear up! The Tamil Nadu Public Service Commission (TNPSC) has released its Annual Planner for 2026, providing a detailed roadmap for various examinations, including the highly anticipated Combined Technical Services (CTC) Exam. This comprehensive guide will walk you through all the crucial dates, eligibility requirements, and important details to help you navigate your preparation effectively for the TNPSC CTC 2026 examinations.</p>

                 <div class="highlight-text">
                     The TNPSC Annual Planner 2026, released on December 3, 2025, serves as the official calendar outlining tentative notification and exam dates for key recruitments, including various Combined Technical Services examinations throughout the year.
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title">Key Exam Dates for TNPSC Combined Technical Services 2026</h2>
                 <p>The Combined Technical Services Examination is conducted for different categories of posts, each with its own schedule. It's crucial to distinguish between them to plan your application and preparation effectively.</p>

                 <h3>1. Combined Technical Services (Interview Posts) II – (Advertisement No. 19/2025)</h3>
                 <p>For those who applied under Advertisement No. 19/2025 for Interview Posts, the exam dates are already set. The application process for these 76 vacancies concluded on January 20, 2026.</p>
                 <div class="benefit-card">
                     <p>✅ <strong>Notification Release:</strong> December 22, 2025</p>
                     <p>✅ <strong>Online Application Window:</strong> December 22, 2025 - January 20, 2026</p>
                     <p>✅ <strong>Application Correction Window:</strong> January 24 - 26, 2026</p>
                     <p>✅ <strong>Admit Card Release (CBT):</strong> February 26, 2026</p>
                     <p>✅ <strong>Computer-Based Test (CBT):</strong> March 7 &amp; 8, 2026</p>
                 </div>

                 <h3>2. Combined Technical Services (Non-Interview Posts)</h3>
                 <p>As per the TNPSC Annual Planner 2026, here are the tentative dates for Non-Interview Posts:</p>
                 <div class="benefit-card">
                     <p>✅ <strong>Tentative Notification Date:</strong> May 20, 2026</p>
                     <p>✅ <strong>Tentative Exam Date:</strong> August 3, 2026 (over 7 days)</p>
                 </div>

                 <h3>3. Combined Technical Services (Diploma / ITI Level)</h3>
                 <p>Candidates with Diploma or ITI qualifications should note the following schedule:</p>
                 <div class="benefit-card">
                     <p>✅ <strong>Tentative Notification Date:</strong> July 7, 2026</p>
                     <p>✅ <strong>Tentative Exam Date:</strong> September 20, 2026 (over 7 days)</p>
                 </div>

                 <h3>4. Combined Technical Services (Interview Posts) – As per Annual Planner</h3>
                 <p>This is a separate recruitment for Interview Posts outlined in the Annual Planner, distinct from the Advertisement No. 19/2025 mentioned above.</p>
                 <div class="benefit-card">
                     <p>✅ <strong>Tentative Notification Date:</strong> August 31, 2026</p>
                     <p>✅ <strong>Tentative Exam Date:</strong> November 14, 2026 (over 4 days)</p>
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title">Comprehensive TNPSC CTC 2026 Schedule</h2>
                 <p>To provide a clearer overview, here's a table summarizing the key dates for the various Combined Technical Services Examinations in 2026:</p>
                 <table>
                     <thead>
                         <tr>
                             <th>Exam Type</th>
                             <th>Notification Date (Tentative)</th>
                             <th>Application Period (Tentative)</th>
                             <th>Admit Card (Tentative)</th>
                             <th>Exam Date (Tentative)</th>
                         </tr>
                     </thead>
                     <tbody>
                         <tr>
                             <td>CTC (Interview Posts) II (Advt. 19/2025)</td>
                             <td>Dec 22, 2025</td>
                             <td>Dec 22, 2025 - Jan 20, 2026</td>
                             <td>Feb 26, 2026</td>
                             <td>Mar 7 &amp; 8, 2026</td>
                         </tr>
                         <tr>
                             <td>CTC (Non-Interview Posts)</td>
                             <td>May 20, 2026</td>
                             <td>(To be announced with notification)</td>
                             <td>(To be announced)</td>
                             <td>Aug 3, 2026 (7 days)</td>
                         </tr>
                         <tr>
                             <td>CTC (Diploma / ITI Level)</td>
                             <td>Jul 7, 2026</td>
                             <td>(To be announced with notification)</td>
                             <td>(To be announced)</td>
                             <td>Sep 20, 2026 (7 days)</td>
                         </tr>
                         <tr>
                             <td>CTC (Interview Posts - Annual Planner)</td>
                             <td>Aug 31, 2026</td>
                             <td>(To be announced with notification)</td>
                             <td>(To be announced)</td>
                             <td>Nov 14, 2026 (4 days)</td>
                         </tr>
                     </tbody>
                 </table>

                 <h2 class="section-title">Eligibility Criteria for TNPSC Combined Technical Services</h2>
                 <p>Before applying, ensure you meet the essential eligibility requirements:</p>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">1. Age Limit</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         Candidates must generally be at least 21 years old. The maximum age limit varies depending on the specific post you are applying for. Age relaxations are applicable for reserved categories.
                     </div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">2. Educational Qualification</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         A degree in a relevant engineering or technical discipline from a recognized university or institution is typically required. Specific posts may require Diploma or ITI qualifications. It's crucial to check the detailed notification for the exact requirements of your desired post.
                     </div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">3. Language Proficiency</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         Proficiency in the Tamil language is mandatory for all applicants.
                     </div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">4. Nationality</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         Applicants must be citizens of India.
                     </div>
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title">Selection Process</h2>
                 <p>The selection process for the TNPSC Combined Technical Services Examination generally involves multiple stages:</p>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">1. Written Examination (Computer-Based Test - CBT)</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         This is the initial stage, assessing candidates on subject-specific technical knowledge, General Studies, and Aptitude and Mental Ability. Paper I usually includes a Tamil Eligibility Test, General Studies, and Aptitude &amp; Mental Ability.
                     </div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">2. Interview / Skill Test</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         Candidates who qualify in the written examination for 'Interview Posts' will be shortlisted for a personal interview or a skill test, depending on the specific requirements of the position.
                     </div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">3. Document Verification</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         Successful candidates from the previous stages will undergo document verification to confirm their eligibility.
                     </div>
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title">How to Stay Updated</h2>
                 <p>The official TNPSC website (www.tnpsc.gov.in) is your primary source for accurate and up-to-date information regarding the Combined Technical Services Examination.</p>
                 <div class="benefit-card">
                     <p>✅ Regularly check the "Annual Planner" section for any revisions or new announcements.</p>
                     <p>✅ Download the official notifications for detailed information on specific posts, syllabi, and application procedures.</p>
                     <p>✅ Ensure you have a One Time Registration (OTR) on the TNPSC website for a smooth application process.</p>
                 </div>

                 <p>With a clear understanding of the TNPSC Combined Technical Services Exam Dates 2026 and the requirements, you can now strategize your preparation effectively. Good luck to all the aspirants!</p>
             </div>
         </div>
   </div>

            
            
